### Step 2: Fetching Real-Time Prices from CoinGecko

The core API call happens in [`fetchAllMarketData()`](file:///d:/blockchain%20min-project/script.js#L60-L143):

```
GET https://api.coingecko.com/api/v3/coins/markets
    ?vs_currency=inr
    &ids=bitcoin,ethereum,solana,...
    &sparkline=true
    &price_change_percentage=24h,7d
    &order=market_cap_desc
    &per_page=12&page=1
```

**What the API returns for each coin:**
| Field | Example Value | Used For |
|-------|-------------|----------|
| `current_price` | 8,743,210 | Showing live price in ₹ |
| `price_change_percentage_24h` | -2.45 | Showing ▲/▼ change badges |
| `market_cap` | 172,000,000,000,000 | Market cap display |
| `total_volume` | 2,800,000,000,000 | 24h volume display |
| `sparkline_in_7d.price` | [87000, 87500, ...] | 7-day mini chart (168 data points) |

**The data is then stored in two objects:**
- **`prices`** — maps coin ID → `{ inr, inr_24h_change, inr_market_cap, inr_24h_vol }`
- **`sparklineData`** — maps coin ID → array of 168 price points (hourly for 7 days)

