### Step 4: Portfolio Rendering & Calculations

When [`displayPortfolio()`](file:///d:/blockchain%20min-project/script.js#L260-L367) runs, it does the following for **each investment**:

```
Investment  = quantity × buyPrice        (what you paid)
Value       = quantity × currentPrice    (what it's worth now)
Profit/Loss = Value - Investment
Return %    = (Profit / Investment) × 100
```

**Example Calculation:**
| Field | Formula | Value |
|-------|---------|-------|
| Quantity | — | 0.5 BTC |
| Buy Price | — | ₹45,00,000 |
| Investment | 0.5 × 45,00,000 | ₹22,50,000 |
| Current Price (live) | — | ₹87,43,210 |
| Current Value | 0.5 × 87,43,210 | ₹43,71,605 |
| Profit | 43,71,605 − 22,50,000 | **+₹21,21,605** |
| Return | (21,21,605 / 22,50,000) × 100 | **+94.29%** |

---

### Step 5: Auto-Refresh Cycle (Every 60 Seconds)

[`startAutoRefresh()`](file:///d:/blockchain%20min-project/script.js#L150-L165) runs a `setInterval` that:
1. Decrements the countdown every second (shown as "30s", "29s", etc. in the header)
2. When countdown hits 0 → calls `fetchAllMarketData()` again
3. All UI updates (ticker, market cards, portfolio table, summary cards) refresh automatically

