## 5. How It Connects to Real-Time Market Prices

```mermaid
flowchart TB
    subgraph "CoinGecko API (Free Tier)"
        A["Aggregates prices from<br/>500+ exchanges worldwide"]
        B["Binance, Coinbase, Kraken,<br/>WazirX, etc."]
    end

    subgraph "Your App"
        C["fetchAllMarketData()"]
        D["prices object"]
        E["UI Components"]
    end

    B --> A
    A -->|"REST API<br/>JSON over HTTPS"| C
    C --> D
    D --> E

    style A fill:#1a1a2e,stroke:#8b5cf6,color:#f1f5f9
    style C fill:#1a1a2e,stroke:#06b6d4,color:#f1f5f9
```

### How CoinGecko Works Behind the Scenes:
1. **CoinGecko** is a crypto data aggregator — it pulls prices from **500+ exchanges** (Binance, Coinbase, Kraken, WazirX, etc.)
2. It calculates a **volume-weighted average price (VWAP)** across all exchanges
3. Your app calls their **free REST API** — no API key required
4. Prices are returned in **INR (₹)** because `vs_currency=inr` is specified
5. Data is **near real-time** (typically 1-2 minute delay from actual exchange prices)

### Rate Limiting & Error Handling:
- CoinGecko's free tier allows ~**10-30 calls/minute**
- Your app refreshes every **60 seconds** (safe within limits)
- If rate-limited (HTTP 429), the app [retries with exponential backoff](file:///d:/blockchain%20min-project/script.js#L79-L92): waits 15s, then 30s, then 45s
- If the API is completely down, cached prices from the last successful call are shown
- Maximum 3 retry attempts before giving up

